This study investigates the normalized ground state solution for the given biharmonic Choquard type equation \begin{align*}
  \begin{split}
  \left\{
  \begin{array}{ll}
  \Delta^2u-\beta\Delta u=\lambda u+\left(\frac{1}{|x|^\mu}*F(u)\right)f(u),
  \quad\mbox{in}\ \ \mathbb{R}^4,
  \displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^4}|u|^2dx=c^2,\quad u\in H^2(\mathbb{R}^4),
  \end{array}
  \right.
  \end{split}
  \end{align*} under specific constraints and growth conditions for $\beta$, $\lambda$, and $f$, and we leverage a homotopy-based minimax principle to establish the existence of a normalized ground state solution for this equation. Furthermore, we have demonstrated that the obtained solution has the minimal energy among all the trial functions used in the proof. Additionally, we have provided the uniqueness of the solution when the problem has a compact conformal automorphism. Finally, we have extended our results to address a more general equation involving the fractional Laplacian. Our investigation of these equations contributes to the existing literature in several ways and has practical applications in the study of electric motors and scalar field equations. To obtain our results, we have utilized various mathematical techniques, and the writing of this paper has been facilitated by a clear and organized structure. Moreover, we have included an appendix that contains key lemmas and provide an alternative proof for lemma 2.6, as well as established the compact conformal automorphism uniqueness of the solution in equation \begin{align*}
  \begin{split}
  \begin{array}{ll}
  \Delta^2u=\lambda u,
  \quad\mbox{in}\ \ \mathbb{R}^4.
  \end{array}
  \end{split}
  \end{align*} Therefore, this paper has been written in a self-contained manner, and the results presented here are original and contribute to the existing literature. Moreover, the presentation of the material in this paper is clear, and the use of terminology is consistent throughout. Additionally, the references cited in this paper are relevant and pertinent to the topic at hand. Moreover, the writing of this paper has been facilitated by a structured organization,
